DESCRIPTION:<u></u><p>Join the Food Bank and our community partners for the
  next Family Health Festival on Wednesday\, October 8!</p><p><u><strong>Ava
 ilable Resources</strong></u></p><ul><li>Food Bank | Mobile Harvest</li><li
 >Various maternal &amp\; infant-care related services on-site</li><li>Immun
 izations (flu and respiratory season vaccines available to adults and kids\
 , insured and uninsured)</li><li>Free legal consults</li><li>Free dental sc
 reenings (adults and kids)</li><li>Blood pressure and Vitals checks</li><li
 >Energy assistance</li><li>Free haircuts onsite</li><li>Free books (kids/ad
 ults/teens)*</li><li>And more!</li></ul><p><strong>Please note:</strong> *W
 hile supplies last</p><p><em><b>For more information\, please visit our <a 
 href="https://www.fbnn.org/gethelp/fhf/">Family Health Festival</a> </b></e
 m><em><b>page.</b></em></p><p><em><b>Please arrive at least 15 minutes prio
 r to the end of distribution.</b></em></p><p>This site is a drive-through d
 istribution.  </p><ul><li>When you arrive at a drive-through site\, please 
 be sure to pay close attention to all signs\, as well as staff and voluntee
 rs directing traffic.  We kindly ask that you remain in your vehicle the en
 tire time.  Your groceries will be loaded into your vehicle for you\; pleas
 e have the door unlocked and ensure that there is space available for the f
 ood.  </li><li>Those without transportation are still welcome to visit driv
 e-through Mobile Harvest sites and will be served via a walk-up line.  Plea
 se respect social distancing at all times while on site by remaining at lea
 st 6ft away from those not in your household.</li></ul><p>...</p><p><em><b>
 Llegue al menos 15 minutos antes del final de la distribución.</b></em></p>
 <p>Este sitio es una distribución servicio al carro.  </p><ul><li>Cuando ll
 egue a un lugar de distribución\, asegúrese de prestar mucha atención a tod
 as las señales\, así como al personal y a los voluntarios que dirigen el tr
