DESCRIPTION:<h3>Family Health Festivals (FHF) are free events that connect 
 the community to local health and community resources\, all in an effort to
  make small steps to a healthier life for all. </h3><br><br>The Family Heal
 th Festival provides an opportunity for the community to connect to a varie
 ty of local education\, employment\, food\, health\, housing\, safety\, and
  transportation resources.  Free services offered at the event will include
  Food Bank Mobile Harvest\, assistance with applying for SNAP (food stamps)
  benefits\, immunizations\, dental screenings\, <span>etc.  </span><br><br>
 The FHF is hosted by a committee of local non-profit\, civic\, and healthca
 re organizations such as Washoe County Health District (WCHD)\, United Way 
 of Northern Nevada and the Sierra\, Immunize Nevada\, Liberty Dental Plan\,
  Food Bank of Northern Nevada (FBNN)\, Molina Healthcare\, Community Servic
 es Agency\, United Health Care\, Northern Nevada Hopes\, and Community Heal
 th Alliance (CHA).
LAST-MODIFIED:20230426T152138Z
LOCATION:Neil Road Recreation Center\, 3925 Neil Rd\, Reno\, NV 89502\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
